    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.ai\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.11.x\n\n### Description\n\nmini.ai does not seem to be able to utilize text-objects from the rewrite of nvim-treesitter and nvim-treesitter-textobjects.\n\nnvim-treesitter has undergone a major breaking rewrite, the `main` branch, removing support for modules. As a result of this, the `master` branch of nvim-treesitter-textobjects is no longer compatible. The new, compatible, version of nvim-treesitter-textobjects is its own `main` branch.\n\nUsing the `main` branch of both nvim-treesitter and nvim-treesitter-textobjects, mini.ai's `gen_spec.treesitter` does not seem to create working keybindings. The `@function` family of objects, `@function.inner` and `@function.outer`, behave more like `@call`. While `@call`, `@loop`, and `@conditional` do not work at all. I have not tried other objects; objects were tested in lua files.\n\n\n\n### Reproduction\n\nMinimal init.lua:\n\n\n```lua\nlocal lazypath = vim.fn.stdpath(\"data\") .. \"/lazy/lazy.nvim\"\nif not (vim.uv or vim.loop).fs_stat(lazypath) then\n  local lazyrepo = \"https://github.com/folke/lazy.nvim.git\"\n  local out = vim.fn.system({ \"git\", \"clone\", \"--filter=blob:none\", \"--branch=stable\", lazyrepo, lazypath })\n  if vim.v.shell_error ~= 0 then\n    vim.api.nvim_echo({\n      { \"Failed to clone lazy.nvim:\\n\", \"ErrorMsg\" },\n      { out,                            \"WarningMsg\" },\n      { \"\\nPress any key to exit...\" },\n    }, true, {})\n    vim.fn.getchar()\n    os.exit(1)\n  end\nend\nvim.opt.rtp:prepend(lazypath)\nrequire(\"lazy\").setup({\n  {\n    \"nvim-treesitter/nvim-treesitter\",\n    lazy = false,\n    build = \":TSUpdate\",\n    branch = \"main\",\n  },\n  {\n    \"nvim-treesitter/nvim-treesitter-textobjects\",\n    depends = \"nvim-treesitter/nvim-treesitter\",\n    lazy = false,\n    branch = \"main\",\n  },\n  {\n    \"echasnovski/mini.nvim\",\n    lazy = false,\n    version = false,\n    config = function()\n      local ts = require(\"mini.ai\").gen_spec.treesitter\n      require(\"mini.ai\").setup({\n        f = ts({ a = \"@function.outer\", i = \"@function.inner\" }),\n        o = ts({ a = \"@conditional.outer\", i = \"@conditional.inner\" }),\n        c = ts({ a = \"@call.outer\", i = \"@call.inner\" }),\n      })\n    end,\n  },\n})\n```\n",
